intuition:
You have 100,000 customer support tickets. You want to know what people are complaining about most without reading all 100,000. Text mining lets you: convert each ticket into a numerical representation, find which words appear unusually often, and cluster the tickets by similarity. You end up with groups like 'payment issues', 'delivery delays', 'product defects' without ever manually labeling a single ticket.

TF-IDF is the core idea. 'The' appears in every ticket — it tells you nothing. 'refund' appears in 15% of tickets and almost nowhere else — it's a signal. TF-IDF weights words by how unique they are to a document relative to the whole collection.

